            "review_title": "Review at Phong Lan Quan",
            "review_text": "kentwallace\nCua Lo, Vietnam140 contributions\n0\nA Tiny Treasure of Yum!\nJul 2018 • Solo\nI recently moved to the Ba Dinh District of Hanoi and was blessed with having this little jewel located but a few doors down.\nThe restaurant is a family affair, with the ever gracious Tu Map (owner and hostess) greeting you at the door, while her brother, the chief chef operates behind the scenes (when he's not helping to serve the meals and drinks).It's a comfort zone for sure...\nThe outdoor patio is my favorite, the canopy of flora, the koi pond, what an atmosphere!\nThe food is excellent and very reasonably priced (think a variety of traditional Vietnamese chicken, steak, salads and stew--with a seafood menu coming soon). \nTu is forever tweaking her menu so you'll never be bored. \nMy hot tip is ask for a glass of her mother's homemade plum/rice wine!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 16, 2018",
